<title>USA: AEP sees Cook 2 nuke increasing power Fri.</title>
<headline>AEP sees Cook 2 nuke increasing power Fri.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>American Electric Power Co's 1,090 megawatt (MW) Cook 2 nuclear power unit in Bridgman, Mich., is expected to begin ramping up later today from its current 55 percent output level, the company said Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;We should be back to full power sometime Sunday,&quot; a company spokesman said.</p>
<p>The unit was holding at a reduced rate to repair a controller on a feedwater pump, he said.</p>
<p>The adjacent unit, with a generating capacity of 1,020 MW, is operating at 94 percent power.</p>
<p>((--New York Power Desk +212-859-1628))</p>
